# The sdist already ships `tests/`, and two of those modules read `scripts/ci.py`
# - `test_ci_catches_faults.py` imports it at module scope, `test_ci_pipeline.py`
# reads it as text. Without this line the published source distribution carries
# the gate's own fault-injection suite and cannot run it: `import ci` raises at
# collection and 12 of 342 tests are uncollectable from the artifact people
# actually download. Measured on trainproof 0.19.0.
#
# `*.py` rather than `graft scripts`, so __pycache__ is never a candidate.
recursive-include scripts *.py
